# Everything the Dockerfile does not need, kept out of the build context.
#
# `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile copies this whole directory, and without a `.dockerignore` that
# includes every project's `bin/` and `obj/` — 300 MB of this developer's build output, shipped to
# the daemon on every build. Worse, `obj/` holds restore artifacts carrying absolute host paths,
# which is a confusing way for a container build to fail.

**/bin
**/obj

# Editor and user state the SDK image neither needs nor reads.
.vs
.vscode
*.user
*.suo
